      en: "The Steam Locomotive Museum in Reșița (Muzeul Locomotivelor cu Abur) is an open-air technical museum. Opened in 1990, it displays over 20 steam locomotives manufactured in Reșița. Reșița was a major locomotive production center in Romania. The locomotives date from 1870 to 1960. The museum is located in the old locomotive depot. Tools and historical photos are also exhibited. It bears witness to the city's industrial past, attracting railway enthusiasts.",
